to minimize these crossings, and these functions are convenience wrappers for
data in formats recognized by \strong{ggalluvial}.

\code{uncross_strata_alluvia()} takes \code{data} in alluvia format (one row per
alluvium, with the axis variables as columns), runs
\code{\link[wompwomp:sort_to_uncross]{wompwomp::sort_to_uncross()}} to obtain a category order at each axis, and
returns the axis variables as factors with levels in these orders.

